<title>FRANCE: BOROTRA DEFENDS RENAULT PLANT CLOSURE.</title>
<headline>BOROTRA DEFENDS RENAULT PLANT CLOSURE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Industry Minister Franck Borotra said on Tuesday that a decision by Renault SA to close a factory in Belgium and cut jobs was needed to reduce costs and return the car operations to break even in 1997 and 1998.</p>
<p>He told parliament during question time that he urged the company to consult with its social partners and follow the law to the letter.</p>
</text>
